      "message": "task_disable_irq() in core/riscv-rv32i/task.c calls chip_disable_irq().\n\nAny boards of chip/mt8192_scp shouldn\u0027t call this function because it is unstable (i.e. chip/mt8192_scp doesn\u0027t support this feature).\n\nI was trying to let developers know: we shouldn\u0027t call this function.\nIf removing the function, when developers accidentally call the function, compiler will complaints about the symbol not found (which is not a good enough clue I think).\n\nWe are thinking to print something via ccprints().  But, I am still considering to print something in chip level??",
